BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Living and Thriving\, Together
DTSTART:20261010T000000
DTEND:20261018T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:76d53c08f1cbd5e2a774094a5ee1f2@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:A joyful examination of how we can make our personal and commu
 nal lives better through collaborative\, connected living. In the antholog
 y Living\, Together: Reimagining Community in the Age of Disconnection\, e
 ditor Samantha Paige Rosen brings together essays about the innovative way
 s people across the country are redefining home and community. In Tiny Gar
 dens Everywhere: The Past\, Present\, and Future of the Self-Provisioning 
 City\, environmental historian Kate Brown presents a “riveting social hi
 story of the world\, as seen through gardens” (Kirkus\, starred). And in
  Friends of the Good: How Remarkable Friendships Transform Our Lives\, Wel
 lWithAll co-founder Demond Martin shares how guiding lights\, mentorship\,
  and kinship shaped his life and how the quality of our friendships determ
 ines who we become. Moderated by Larry Gennari\, founder and curator of Au
 thors & Innovators. Books sold by Wellesley Books. LEARN MORE Sources: Mee
 t Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/living-and-thriving-
 together/93619/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01
 532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page:
  https://www.meetboston.com/event/living-and-thriving-together/93619/
LOCATION:Boston Public Library - Rabb Hall\, Boston Public Library - Rabb 
 Hall 700 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/living-and-thriving-together/93619/
END:VEVENT
