 wntown Worcester on Saturday\, October 10 for an afternoon and evening cel
 ebrating **music\, art and community**. Hosted at Off The Rails\, Woostock
  brings together an eclectic lineup of Worcester-area musicians alongside 
 local artists\, makers\, food vendors\, small businesses and community org
 anizations for a festival built around the creative community that makes W
 orcester special. Expect live music throughout the day\, local art and ven
 dors to explore\, food and drinks\, and plenty of opportunities to discove
 r the people and projects shaping Worcester's creative scene. This year's 
 festival begins before guests even reach the stage: attendees will enter t
 hrough a colorful art installation created from hand-painted vinyl records
  made collaboratively by Woostock musicians\, artists\, vendors\, voluntee
 rs and their families. Woostock will also include a special tribute to the
  late Worcester musician **Jorge “Tasteless Jack” Ramirez**\, with his
  friends taking his scheduled festival slot to celebrate his life and musi
 c. Whether you come for a favorite band or to discover something new\, Woo
 stock is an invitation to spend the day experiencing Worcester through the
  people who make\, play\, create and contribute here. **Music • Art • 
 Community.** Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://w
 ww.discovercentralma.org/event/woostock-2026-(year-2)/30766/\n\nEvents Nea
