SUMMARY:Watertown Indigenous Peoples Day Celebration
DTSTART:20261011T000000
DTEND:20261011T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:3302792af6be555f6dbaacb952b545@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Watertown’s fifth celebration of Indigenous Peoples Day will
  be held on Sunday\, Oct. 11\, 2026\, from 12 to 3 p.m. at the Hosmer Elem
 entary School\, 1 Concord Road\, Watertown\, MA. The free event will featu
 re Indigenous musicians\, artists and vendors. The Wampanoag Nation Singer
 s and Dancers will share traditional songs and dances (1 – 2 p.m.). Arti
 sans Darius Coombs and Eleanor Coombs\, Mashpee Wampanoag \, will be demon
 strating how to create wampum and corn husk dolls (12 – 2:30 p.m.). Part
 icipants will be able to make their own corn husk dolls. James Beard award
  winner Chef Sherry Pocknett\, Mashpee Wampanoag \, will meet with culinar
 y arts students at Watertown High School on Friday\, Oct. 9th providing an
  introduction to Indigenous food and traditions. She will work with the st
 udents as they prepare some of her award winning Indigenous dishes that wi
 ll be available at Sunday’s Indigenous Peoples Day celebration. Indigeno
 us vendors include: Claudia Fox Tree\, Arawak-Taino iukaieke Guainia \, Ar
 awak Designs\, Linda Coombs\, Aquinnah Wampanoag \, Leslie Tuplin\, First 
 Nation Mi’kmaq-Lennox Island – PEI \, Native Solutions and Cindy Shell
 ey\, Up the Creek Traders. Belmont Bookstore will be selling books by and 
 about Indigenous people and the Watertown Free Library Bookmobile will hav
 e books about Indigenous people to borrow. Sources: Meet Boston Event page
 : https://www.meetboston.com/event/watertown-indigenous-peoples-day-celebr
 ation/93593/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532
 \nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: ht
 tps://www.meetboston.com/event/watertown-indigenous-peoples-day-celebratio
 n/93593/
LOCATION:Hosmer Elementary School\, Hosmer Elementary School 1 Concord Roa
 d\, Watertown\, MA\, 02472
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/watertown-indigenous-peoples-day-cele
 bration/93593/
END:VEVENT
