BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Operation Mincemeat: A New Musical
DTSTART:20261013T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:61e7081849fea7c6f08b9d6650a5e2@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:How did a dead body\, a fake love letter\, and — of all peop
 le — Ian Fleming turn the tide of WWII? Olivier Award winner for Best Ne
 w Musical and a 2025 Tony(r) winner\, Operation Mincemeat: A New Musical i
 s the best-reviewed show in West End history with 88 five-star reviews and
  the #1 Broadway Show of 2025 (Entertainment Weekly). It’s 1943 and the 
 Allies are on the ropes. Luckily\, they’re about to gamble our futures o
 n a stolen corpse. Singin’ in the Rain meets Strangers on a Train\, it
 ’s the fast-paced\, hilarious true story of the secret mission that won 
 WWII. Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/op
 eration-mincemeat%3a-a-new-musical/88989/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mil
 es of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusett
 s-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/operation-minc
 emeat%3a-a-new-musical/88989/
LOCATION:Emerson Colonial Theatre\, 106 Boylston Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02
 116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/operation-mincemeat%3a-a-new-musical/
 88989/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pınar Öğrenci
DTSTART:20261013T000000
DTEND:20261013T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:83ace0f287580566f4a6a1ff6e7e44@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Berlin-based artist and filmmaker Pınar Öğrenci will discus
 s her 2024 film Glück auf in Deutschland (Good Luck in Germany)\, which i
 s featured in her first major exhibition in the United States\, here at th
 e Harvard Art Museums. The film examines the construction of postwar Germa
 n identity in the Ruhrgebiet\, a heavily industrialized region known for c
 oal mining and steel production\, as shaped by layered experiences of surv
 ival\, resistance\, and resilience. In it\, Öğrenci applies a feminist l
 ens\, broadening the history of industrial labor beyond the male worker an
 d the factory. The lecture brings Glück auf in Deutschland into conversat
 ion with Öğrenci’s other films\, exploring filmmaking as a political p
 ractice through which the history of “guest workers” can be connected 
 to ongoing struggles around labor\, migration\, and belonging. The exhibit
 ion Pınar Öğrenci: Glück auf in Deutschland (April 16\, 2026–October
  18\, 2026) includes the 2024 film Glück auf in Deutschland (Good Luck in
  Germany) as well as five related collages that reimagine the bodies of wo
 rkers and their families within the Ruhr landscape and its architecture. 
 Öğrenci’s use of the phrase Glück auf —a common way that miners wis
 h one another a safe return after their physically grueling and dangerous 
 work underground—resonates with the experiences of immigrant communities
  in present-day Germany facing right-wing extremism. Following the program
 \, guests are invited to visit the exhibition on Level 1. LEARN MORE Sourc
 es: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/p%c4%b1nar-%c
 3%96%c4%9frenci/93547/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough
 \, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSour
 ce page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/p%c4%b1nar-%c3%96%c4%9frenci/935
 47/
LOCATION:Harvard Art Museums\, Harvard Art Museums 32 Quincy Street\, Camb
 ridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/p%c4%b1nar-%c3%96%c4%9frenci/93547/
END:VEVENT
