BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Tobacco Takers: Puritans\, Pipes\, and Bodily Care
DTSTART:20261013T000000
DTEND:20261013T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:a477f8e3d47ae8f04becfeeb34062e@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Indigenous to the Americas and cultivated by Native peoples fo
 r thousands of years\, tobacco was introduced to Europeans in the 16th cen
 tury\, and by the early 17th century\, it had spread across the globe. In 
 Puritan New England\, religious leaders condemned tobacco as sinful while 
 early practitioners used it as medicine. Clay tobacco pipes commonly found
  at 17th-century archaeological sites in Massachusetts reveal widespread u
 se despite strict social and religious restrictions. Drawing from her new 
 book\, The Tobacco Takers: Puritanism\, Smoking\, Health\, and the Archaeo
 logy of Bodily Care (Bloomsbury Publishing\, 2026)\, Diana DiPaolo Loren\,
  deputy director for curatorial affairs and senior curator at Harvard’s 
 Peabody Museum\, will share archaeological\, archival\, and visual evidenc
 e that recasts tobacco and tobacco pipes as tools of bodily care for both 
 physical and metaphysical ailments. The program will include a conversatio
 n with archaeologist Stephen W. Silliman. Copies of The Tobacco Takers wil
 l be available for purchase after the program. Advance registration is rec
 ommended. Free event parking is available with registration at the 52 Oxfo
 rd Street Garage\, starting at 5:00 pm. Register by October 12th\, 2026 to
  receive parking registration instructions. Presented by the Peabody Museu
 m of Archaeology & Ethnology and the Harvard Museums of Science & Culture.
  LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.mee
 tboston.com/event/the-tobacco-takers%3a-puritans-pipes-and-bodily-care/932
 95/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscove
 ry: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www
 .meetboston.com/event/the-tobacco-takers%3a-puritans-pipes-and-bodily-care
 /93295/
LOCATION:Geological Lecture Hall\, Geological Lecture Hall\, Harvard Museu
 m of the Ancient Near East 24 Oxford Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-tobacco-takers%3a-puritans-pipes-
 and-bodily-care/93295/
END:VEVENT
