BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston Book Festival Opening Night: Michael Lewis
DTSTART:20261016T000000
DTEND:20261016T000000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:71ec06c8f8fbfc59f4e86fa229708f@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Boston Book Festival is pleased to present #1 New York Tim
 es bestselling author Michael Lewis\, in-conversation with Pulitzer Prize 
 winner Geraldine Brooks\, author of Memorial Days\, discussing Lewis’s h
 ighly anticipated Blockers: Rebels in the Deep State. A masterful storytel
 ler with the remarkable ability to make any subject – from subprime mort
 gages (The Big Short) to baseball statistics (Moneyball) to bond sales (Li
 ar’s Poker) – riveting\, Michael Lewis’s Blockers offers an inside l
 ook at the early days of Trump’s Department of Government Efficiency (DO
 GE) and asks the pressing question: “What happens to a country when its 
 public servants are targeted?” Lewis views the “meteor strike” of th
 e second Trump administration through the eyes of public servants attacked
  by DOGE – including one who kept Americans’ most sensitive tax data o
 ut of the wrong hands\; another who made sure that politicians played by t
 he rules\; one who figured out how to stop wildfires from destroying subur
 ban neighborhoods\; and another who helped uncover the mysteries of cystic
  fibrosis. Each believed they had a calling and were doing essential work 
 for the country. They were then told they were a “blocker:” an impedim
 ent\, a holdover\, someone useless who needed to go. The Boston Book Festi
 val gathers the Greater Boston community together with authors around the 
 transformative joys of reading\, the power of stories\, and the exchange o
 f ideas through a wide range of free programming. This year’s Festival w
 ill take place on Saturday\, October 17 and will feature 300+ authors\, il
 lustrators\, and exhibitors. This Festival is only possible with community
  support. Please consider adding a donation of any amount to your ticket p
 urchase to help keep the festival free and open to all. All tickets includ
 e a signed hardcover of Blockers: Rebels in the Deep State\, which will be
  distributed at the event. Those unable to attend can pick up their book a
 t Harvard Book Store within 30 days following the event. MORE INFORMATION 
 / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/
 event/boston-book-festival-opening-night%3a-michael-lewis/93583/\n\nEvents
  Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fal
 lback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.c
 om/event/boston-book-festival-opening-night%3a-michael-lewis/93583/
LOCATION:Old South Church\, Old South Church 645 Boylston Street\, Boston
 \, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-book-festival-opening-night%3a
 -michael-lewis/93583/
END:VEVENT
