BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kayla Schwartz\, Graphic Designer “Get With The Action! Corita K
 ent and Typography as a Tool for Civic Engagement” | HumanArts
DTSTART:20261029T190000
DTEND:20261029T203000
DTSTAMP:20261010T163808Z
UID:61a88f229e43da5bcdbe55b5b0779b@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:October 29\, 2026\, 7:00 PM\, Kennedy 112 For as long as peopl
 e have had walls\, we have put marks on them. In this talk\, environmental
  graphic designer Kayla Schwartz presents typography’s power to shape ci
 vilization and the long human habit of making meaning visible: from cave p
 aintings to cuneiform\, moveable type to road signs\, the “I Voted” st
 icker to the ballot itself. She shares student work from her new course\, 
 Design for Civic Engagement\, which centers the work of Corita Kent—the 
 artist\, educator\, nun\, and activist whose exuberant screenprints turned
  supermarket slogans into arguments for peace and justice in the 1960s—a
 round the objective of increasing civic engagement through nonpartisan typ
 ographic activation on campus. Source: Assumption University Event page: h
 ttps://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/kayla-schwartz-graphic-de
 signer-get-with-the-action-corita-kent-and-typography-as-a-tool-for-civic-
 engagement-humanarts\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, 
 MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester-colleges-events.ics\nSo
 urce page: https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/kayla-schwart
 z-graphic-designer-get-with-the-action-corita-kent-and-typography-as-a-too
 l-for-civic-engagement-humanarts
LOCATION:Kennedy Hall Room 112\, 500 Salisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1609
URL:https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/kayla-schwartz-graph
 ic-designer-get-with-the-action-corita-kent-and-typography-as-a-tool-for-c
 ivic-engagement-humanarts
END:VEVENT
